{"nodes": [{"id": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_nestjs_principles", "label": "NestJS principles and templates", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".claude/skills/backend-developer/references/nestjs-principles.md", "source_location": "# NestJS principles and templates", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_configservice", "label": "ConfigService", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/backend-developer/references/nestjs-principles.md", "source_location": "## 8. Configuration", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Read settings with ConfigService.getOrThrow so they are validated, typed, and testable. process.env inside a service bypasses the Joi schema and is invisible to tests."}, {"id": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_request_pipeline", "label": "NestJS request pipeline", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/backend-developer/references/nestjs-principles.md", "source_location": "## 1. Mental model", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Order is Express middleware, route match, guards, interceptors before the handler, pipes, the handler, interceptors after, then exception filters. A guard sees the raw request because pipes have not run. Middleware registered in main.ts also runs for unmatched routes."}, {"id": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_secure_by_default", "label": "Secure by default", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/backend-developer/references/nestjs-principles.md", "source_location": "## 5. Guards, custom decorators, and authorization", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Register the auth guard globally with APP_GUARD and opt out with @Public(), so a forgotten decorator fails closed. Authentication and authorization are different guards. Resource ownership is checked in the service because it needs data."}, {"id": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_fail_fast_configuration", "label": "Fail-fast configuration", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/backend-developer/references/nestjs-principles.md", "source_location": "## 8. Configuration", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Secrets the app cannot run without are required() in the Joi schema. A default such as postgresql://localhost/mock lets a mis-set production environment start successfully and fail later."}, {"id": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_prisma_p2002", "label": "Prisma P2002", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/backend-developer/references/nestjs-principles.md", "source_location": "## 9. Persistence with Prisma", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Race-proof uniqueness with a unique index and catch Prisma P2002, instead of check-then-insert."}, {"id": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_enableshutdownhooks", "label": "enableShutdownHooks", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/backend-developer/references/nestjs-principles.md", "source_location": "## 11. Lifecycle, shutdown, and health", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SIGTERM and SIGINT run onModuleDestroy only after enableShutdownHooks(). Without it, containers are killed mid-request and the DB, Redis, and queue workers are not closed."}, {"id": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_trust_proxy", "label": "trust proxy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/backend-developer/references/nestjs-principles.md", "source_location": "## 15. Express 5 / Nest 11 gotchas", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Behind a proxy, set trust proxy before using req.ip. A client-supplied X-Forwarded-For is spoofable and must not be the rate-limit key."}, {"id": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_raw_byte_hmac", "label": "Raw-byte HMAC", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/backend-developer/references/nestjs-principles.md", "source_location": "## 5. Guards, custom decorators, and authorization", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Signature and HMAC guards must hash the raw bytes received, not JSON.stringify(body), and compare with timingSafeEqual. Add a timestamp window and a nonce store to stop replays."}, {"id": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_integer_money", "label": "Integer money", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/backend-developer/references/nestjs-principles.md", "source_location": "## 9. Persistence with Prisma", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Do not use floats for token amounts. BigInt is not JSON-serializable; convert to a string at the boundary and never Number(), because JSON numbers lose precision above 2^53."}, {"id": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_idempotent_queue_jobs", "label": "Idempotent queue jobs", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/backend-developer/references/nestjs-principles.md", "source_location": "## 10. Queues and background jobs (BullMQ)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A job can run more than once. Use a deterministic jobId, unique constraints, and status checks. Transient errors retry; permanent failures throw UnrecoverableError. Keep failed jobs for inspection."}, {"id": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_liveness_versus_readiness", "label": "Liveness versus readiness", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/backend-developer/references/nestjs-principles.md", "source_location": "## 11. Lifecycle, shutdown, and health", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Liveness returns 200 when the process is up and must not check dependencies. Readiness checks DB, Redis, and critical upstreams with short timeouts and returns 503 when not ready."}, {"id": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_provide_a_provider_once", "label": "Provide a provider once", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/backend-developer/references/nestjs-principles.md", "source_location": "## 2. Modules and dependency injection", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never list the same provider in two modules. Nest creates two instances, each with its own state. Provide once, export, and import. The documented example is OtpRateLimitService in both RedisModule and OtpModule."}, {"id": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_express_5_global_prefix_wildcard", "label": "Express 5 global prefix wildcard", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/backend-developer/references/nestjs-principles.md", "source_location": "## 15. Express 5 / Nest 11 gotchas", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Express 5 path-to-regexp v8 rejects bare star wildcards. The repo's setGlobalPrefix exclude uses a pattern like /.well-known/(.*); confirm it still behaves on the installed version."}], "edges": [{"source": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_raw_byte_hmac", "target": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_honebill_backend_review_webhook_authentication", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": ".claude/skills/backend-developer/references/nestjs-principles.md", "source_location": "## 5. Guards, custom decorators, and authorization", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_configservice", "target": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_honebill_backend_walkthrough_env_validation", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/skills/backend-developer/references/nestjs-principles.md", "source_location": "## 8. Configuration", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_idempotent_queue_jobs", "target": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_honebill_backend_walkthrough_unrecoverableerror", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": ".claude/skills/backend-developer/references/nestjs-principles.md", "source_location": "## 10. Queues and background jobs (BullMQ)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_secure_by_default", "target": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_request_pipeline", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": ".claude/skills/backend-developer/references/nestjs-principles.md", "source_location": "## 5. Guards, custom decorators, and authorization", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_nestjs_principles_provide_a_provider_once", "target": "claude_skills_backend_developer_references_honebill_backend_walkthrough_otpratelimitservice", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/skills/backend-developer/references/nestjs-principles.md", "source_location": "## 2. Modules and dependency injection", "weight": 1.0}, {